==English==

===Etymology===
< {{etyl|la}} {{term|circulatus}}, past participle of {{term|circulare||make circular, encircle}}, a later collateral form of {{term|circulari||form a circle (of men) around one's self}} < {{term|circulus||a circle}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|En-us-circulate.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|circulat|ing}}

# {{intransitive}} to [[move]] in [[circle]]s or through a [[circuit]]
# {{transitive}} to cause (a person or thing) to move in [[circle]]s or through a [[circuit]]
# to move from [[person]] to person, as at a [[party]]
# to [[spread]] or [[disseminate]]
# to become [[widely]] [[known]]

====Synonyms====
* [[put about]]
* [[spread]]
* [[disseminate]]

